# CSS Best Practices & Component Scoping

## Purpose and Scope

This rule enforces CSS Module standards, component scoping patterns, and performance optimization for the Broken Loop Brewing website. It ensures consistent styling architecture, prevents CSS conflicts, and maintains high performance through proper CSS practices.

## Standards and Requirements

### CSS Module Requirements - STRICTLY ENFORCE

#### File Structure Requirements
```
src/components/ComponentName/
  ├── ComponentName.tsx
  └── ComponentName.module.css
```

#### CSS Module Class Usage
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - CSS Modules
import styles from './Component.module.css';

export function Component({ variant = 'default' }) {
  const componentClass = variant === 'primary' 
    ? styles.componentPrimary 
    : styles.component;
    
  return (
    <div className={componentClass}>
      <h2 className={styles.title}>Title</h2>
      <div className={styles.content}>Content</div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ INCORRECT - Global classes
export function Component() {
  return (
    <div className="component"> {/* ❌ Global class */}
      <h2 className="title">Title</h2> {/* ❌ Global class */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### Global CSS Restrictions
- **globals.css**: ONLY CSS resets, typography, and CSS custom properties
- **variables.css**: ONLY :root custom properties
- **NO** component-specific styles in global files
- **NO** utility classes (use CSS Modules instead)

### CSS Best Practices - STRICTLY ENFORCE

#### NEVER Use `!important`
> **Reference**: See [CSS No Important Rule](./cssNoImportant.mdc) for detailed guidance on avoiding `!important` and managing CSS specificity.

- **NEVER** use `!important` declarations - refactor specificity instead
- Use CSS Modules scoping to prevent conflicts
- Use CSS custom properties for overrides
- Follow proper cascade order

#### CSS Property Order
1. **Display & positioning**
2. **Box model** (width, height, padding, margin)
3. **Typography**
4. **Visual** (background, border, shadow)
5. **Animations & transitions**

#### Forbidden Patterns
- ❌ `!important` declarations
- ❌ Global CSS classes for components
- ❌ Inline styles (except dynamic values)
- ❌ Deep selector nesting (max 2 levels)
- ❌ Fixed z-index values (use CSS custom properties)
- ❌ Magic numbers (use named variables)

#### Required Patterns
- ✅ CSS Modules for all component styles
- ✅ CSS custom properties for reusable values
- ✅ Semantic class names
- ✅ Mobile-first responsive design
- ✅ Consistent spacing scale
- ✅ Proper accessibility (focus states, contrast)

### Advanced CSS Module Patterns

#### CSS Module Composition
```css
/* Base.module.css */
.button {
  padding: var(--spacing-sm) var(--spacing-md);
  border: none;
  border-radius: var(--border-radius);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all var(--transition-speed) ease;
}

/* Button.module.css */
.primaryButton {
  composes: button from './Base.module.css';
  background: var(--color-primary);
  color: white;
}

.secondaryButton {
  composes: button from './Base.module.css';
  background: var(--color-secondary);
  color: white;
}
```

#### Dynamic Class Names
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Dynamic class composition
const getComponentClasses = (variant: string, size: string, className?: string) => {
  const baseClass = styles.component;
  const variantClass = styles[`component${variant.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + variant.slice(1)}`];
  const sizeClass = styles[`component${size.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + size.slice(1)}`];
  
  return [baseClass, variantClass, sizeClass, className]
    .filter(Boolean)
    .join(' ');
};

// Usage
<div className={getComponentClasses('primary', 'large', customClass)}>
  Content
</div>
```

#### CSS Module with TypeScript
```typescript
// ComponentName.d.ts
export interface ComponentNameProps {
  variant?: 'default' | 'primary' | 'secondary';
  size?: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large';
  className?: string;
  children?: React.ReactNode;
}

// ComponentName.tsx
import styles from './ComponentName.module.css';

export const ComponentName: React.FC<ComponentNameProps> = ({
  variant = 'default',
  size = 'medium',
  className = '',
  children,
  ...props
}) => {
  const componentClasses = [
    styles.component,
    styles[`component${variant.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + variant.slice(1)}`],
    styles[`component${size.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + size.slice(1)}`],
    className
  ].filter(Boolean).join(' ');

  return (
    <div className={componentClasses} {...props}>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
};
```

### Performance Optimization

#### CSS Performance Best Practices
```css
/* ✅ GOOD - Use will-change sparingly */
.animatedElement {
  will-change: transform; /* Only for elements that will actually change */
}

/* ✅ GOOD - Use contain for isolated components */
.isolatedComponent {
  contain: layout style paint; /* Isolate component rendering */
}

/* ✅ GOOD - GPU-accelerated animations */
.smoothAnimation {
  transform: translateZ(0); /* Force GPU acceleration */
  transition: transform var(--transition-speed) ease;
}
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD - Avoid layout thrashing */
.badAnimation {
  width: 100px;
  height: 100px;
  /* Don't animate width/height - use transform instead */
}
```

#### Critical CSS Patterns
```css
/* ✅ GOOD - Critical CSS for above-the-fold content */
.heroSection {
  /* Inline critical styles */
  background: var(--color-primary);
  padding: var(--spacing-xl) 0;
  min-height: 60vh;
}

/* ✅ GOOD - Defer non-critical styles */
.nonCriticalStyles {
  /* Load these styles asynchronously */
  display: none; /* Hidden until loaded */
}
```

### Accessibility in CSS

#### Focus Management
```css
/* ✅ GOOD - Visible focus indicators */
.interactiveElement:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-primary);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

/* ✅ GOOD - High contrast focus states */
.button:focus-visible {
  background: var(--color-primary);
  color: white;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--color-background), 0 0 0 4px var(--color-primary);
}
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD - Remove focus outline */
.button:focus {
  outline: none; /* ❌ Never remove focus outline without replacement */
}
```

#### Reduced Motion Support
```css
/* ✅ GOOD - Respect user preferences */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .animatedElement {
    animation: none;
    transition: none;
  }
  
  .smoothScroll {
    scroll-behavior: auto;
  }
}
```

#### High Contrast Mode
```css
/* ✅ GOOD - High contrast mode support */
@media (prefers-contrast: high) {
  .card {
    border: 2px solid var(--color-text);
    background: var(--color-background);
  }
  
  .button {
    border: 2px solid currentColor;
  }
}
```

### Error Prevention & Validation

#### CSS Module Import Validation
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Validate CSS Module imports
import styles from './Component.module.css';

// TypeScript will catch missing classes at compile time
const componentClass = styles.component; // Error if .component doesn't exist
```

#### CSS Linting Rules
```json
// .stylelintrc.json
{
  "rules": {
    "declaration-no-important": true,
    "selector-max-depth": 2,
    "selector-max-specificity": "0,3,0",
    "declaration-block-no-duplicate-properties": true,
    "declaration-block-no-redundant-longhand-properties": true
  }
}
```

#### Build-time Validation
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Validate CSS custom properties usage
const validateCSSProperties = () => {
  const styleSheets = Array.from(document.styleSheets);
  
  styleSheets.forEach(sheet => {
    try {
      const rules = Array.from(sheet.cssRules);
      rules.forEach(rule => {
        if (rule instanceof CSSStyleRule) {
          // Check for hardcoded colors
          if (rule.style.color && !rule.style.color.includes('var(--')) {
            console.warn('Hardcoded color found:', rule.selectorText);
          }
        }
      });
    } catch (e) {
      // Cross-origin stylesheets will throw
    }
  });
};
```

